title: "FoC — Supplier Service: add a bookmark (N8, D10, D14)"
---
%% AI-assisted (CS3219 AI Usage Policy disclosure):
%% Tool: Claude Code (Sonnet 5.5), 2026-11-10, issue #326.
%% Scope: sequence diagram of PUT /suppliers/{id}/bookmark, transcribed from
%% BookmarkController, BookmarkService and BookmarkLock and from the
%% author's decisions D10 (cap of 5, 409) and D14 (per-user advisory lock,
%% 409 "too fast", not retried) in docs/supplier-service.md. Transcription
%% only; no design decision made by the tool.
%% Author review: Alastair Tan Choon Wei to review via pull request.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as Signed-in user
    participant W as Web App
    participant G as API Gateway
    participant B as Bookmark API (BookmarkService)
    participant L as BookmarkLock
    participant DB as Supplier DB (PostgreSQL)

    U->>W: click the bookmark flag on a supplier
    W->>G: PUT /api/supplier/suppliers/{id}/bookmark (bearer JWT)
    G->>B: PUT /suppliers/{id}/bookmark
    Note over B: user id = verified JWT subject,<br/>never taken from the request
    B->>DB: find supplier by id
    alt supplier does not exist
        B-->>W: 404 problem+json
    else supplier exists
        Note over B,DB: one transaction from here
        B->>L: tryLock(userId)
        L->>DB: SELECT pg_try_advisory_xact_lock(userId)
        alt lock not acquired (parallel add by the same user)
            B-->>W: 409 "You are bookmarking too fast, please try again."<br/>(nothing saved, not retried, D14)
        else lock acquired
            B->>DB: find bookmark (userId, supplierId) and count the user's bookmarks
            alt already bookmarked
                B-->>W: 200 existing bookmark, count unchanged<br/>(no-op, does not count against the cap)
            else count is already 5
                B-->>W: 409 "You have reached the limit of 5 bookmarks." (D10)
            else room left
                B->>DB: insert bookmark and flush
                alt foreign key violation (supplier deleted since the lookup)
                    B-->>W: 404 problem+json
                else saved
                    B-->>W: 200 {supplierId, bookmarked, bookmarkedAt, count}
                end
            end
        end
        Note over B,DB: commit or rollback releases the advisory lock
    end
    W-->>U: star shown, or the error message
